    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d502">

                <pb facs="0766" n="738" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg738"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">310.2/7–854: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative at the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lodge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">limited official use</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-07-08T16:00:00-04:00">July 8, 1954—4
                            p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>16. Re admission Communist China. Ardalan (Iran) says he is strongly opposed to
                    seating of Communist China. Serrano (Philippines) says he is against it but
                    questioned our intention to go through. Forsyth (Australia) was surprised and
                    shocked by Foreign Minister Webb of New Zealand’s declaration in favor of
                    admitting Communist China.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lodge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
